# SafeVisionAI

## AI-Based Real-Time Worker Safety Monitoring System

SafeVisionAI is a computer vision-based worker safety monitoring system designed to detect PPE compliance violations from video streams and camera feeds.

The system uses YOLO-based object detection to identify workers and safety equipment, detect safety-rule violations, record violation events, and provide visual evidence through a Streamlit monitoring dashboard.

## Features

* YOLO-based PPE detection
* Worker safety monitoring
* Helmet detection
* Safety vest detection
* Safety boots detection
* Gloves detection
* Goggles detection
* Safety violation detection
* Video file testing
* Webcam/camera support
* Video stream/source URL support
* Violation logging
* Automatic screenshot capture for violations
* Streamlit monitoring dashboard
* Employee details management

## System Workflow

```text
Video / Camera Source
        ↓
Video Processing
        ↓
YOLO Object Detection
        ↓
Object Tracking
        ↓
Safety Rule Checking
        ↓
Violation Detection
        ↓
Violation Logging
        ↓
Screenshot Capture
        ↓
Streamlit Dashboard
```

## Project Structure

```text
SafeVisionAI/
│
├── dashboard.py
├── test_pipeline.py
├── data_manager.py
├── requirements.txt
├── README.md
│
├── pages/
│   └── employee_details.py
│
└── models/
    └── best.pt
```

The trained model is provided separately through the GitHub Release because of its file size.

## Installation

### 1. Clone the Repository

```bash
git clone https://github.com/Shahmeerkhan037/SafeVisionAI---PPE-DETECTION.git
cd SafeVisionAI---PPE-DETECTION
```

### 2. Create a Virtual Environment

It is recommended to use a virtual environment.

```bash
python -m venv .venv
```

Activate it on Windows:

```bash
.venv\Scripts\activate
```

### 3. Install Dependencies

Install the required Python packages:

```bash
pip install -r requirements.txt
```

The main dependencies include:

* Ultralytics
* OpenCV
* NumPy
* Pandas
* Streamlit
* Pillow

## Model Setup

The trained YOLO model is available in the **Releases** section of this GitHub repository.

Download the `best.pt` model from the latest release.

After downloading the model, place it wherever you prefer on your computer.

Then open:

```text
test_pipeline.py
```

and enter the path to the downloaded model.

Example:

```python
MODEL_PATH = "models/best.pt"
```

You can also use an absolute path:

```python
MODEL_PATH = r"C:\path\to\best.pt"
```

## Configuring the Video Source

The video source is also configured in:

```text
test_pipeline.py
```

### Demo Video

To test the model on a video file:

```python
VIDEO_SOURCE = "demo_video.mp4"
```

Or use an absolute path:

```python
VIDEO_SOURCE = r"C:\path\to\demo_video.mp4"
```

### Webcam

To use the default camera:

```python
VIDEO_SOURCE = 0
```

For another connected camera:

```python
VIDEO_SOURCE = 1
```

### Video Stream / Camera URL

If a supported network camera or video stream URL is available:

```python
VIDEO_SOURCE = "YOUR_VIDEO_SOURCE_URL"
```

## Employee Details

Create a folder named:

```text
pages
```

Inside the folder, place:

```text
employee_details.py
```

The structure should be:

```text
pages/
└── employee_details.py
```

Streamlit will use this file as an additional dashboard page.

## Running the Dashboard

Start the Streamlit dashboard with:

```bash
streamlit run dashboard.py
```

Streamlit will provide a local URL where the dashboard can be accessed.

The dashboard displays recorded safety violations and their captured screenshots.

## Testing the Model

After configuring `MODEL_PATH` and `VIDEO_SOURCE` inside `test_pipeline.py`, run:

```bash
python test_pipeline.py
```

The system will process the selected video, webcam, or supported video source.

During processing, detected safety violations will be recorded.

## Violation Recording

When a person is detected as violating a safety rule, the system records the violation.

A screenshot is captured as visual evidence of the violation.

The recorded violation and its screenshot can then be viewed through the Streamlit dashboard.

The overall process is:

```text
Person Detected
      ↓
PPE Detection
      ↓
Safety Rules Checked
      ↓
Violation Detected
      ↓
Violation Logged
      ↓
Screenshot Captured
      ↓
Violation Displayed on Dashboard
```

